From 74c8f703a93ebbbd219821f10e69d1c540cc052c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Popov <nikita.ppv@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ext/soap: SAFE_STR casts to const char * (follow-up to
 CVE-2021-21702)

The CVE-2021-21702 backport added SAFE_STR(a) ((a)?a:""). With an
xmlChar * argument the two branches have different pointer types, which
newer gcc rejects (an error without -fpermissive). The upstream build fix
casts the pointer.

Backport of php-src e5d767d27f (Nikita Popov), same change as Sury's 7.2
patch 0060; part of fajxo/issue-tracking#205 batch A+B.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/soap/php_sdl.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/soap/php_sdl.c b/ext/soap/php_sdl.c
index b8d40f0c..522db1c9 100644
--- a/ext/soap/php_sdl.c
+++ b/ext/soap/php_sdl.c
@@ -314,7 +314,7 @@ void sdl_restore_uri_credentials(sdlCtx *ctx)
 	ctx->context = NULL;
 }
 
-#define SAFE_STR(a) ((a)?a:"")
+#define SAFE_STR(a) ((a)?((const char *)a):"")
 
 static void load_wsdl_ex(zval *this_ptr, char *struri, sdlCtx *ctx, int include)
 {
